          "path": "_m/d/p/z/8/casa-loma-wp/1924-dodge-model-d2-to.jpg",
          "filename": "DSC09026 - 1924 Dodge Model D2 Touring Sedan (36823715580).jpg",
          "caption": "1924 Dodge Model D2 Touring Sedan\n1924 is the year that Case was abandoned.\nFour Cylinder, Thirty-five horsepower.\nAll steel body - a specialty of the Dodge Brothers and one of the firsts for its time. An affordable everyman’s car, Dodge still managed a few upscale touches: solid wheels, running board steps, a taller grille design that was new for 1924. In addition, this one even wears double bumpers that were an option. And in the rear: roll down windows, heat vent and sunshades.\n\n\nThe Carriage Room and Garage features vintage automobiles from the early 1900s as well as some old carriages.",
          "alt": "1924 Dodge Model D2 Touring Sedan\n1924 is the year that Case was abandoned.\nFour Cylinder, Thirty-five horsepower.\nAll steel body - a specialty of the Dodge Brothers and one of the firsts for its time. An affordable everyman’s car, Dodge still managed a few upscale touches: solid wheels, running board steps, a taller grille design that was new for 1924. In addition, this one even wears double bumpers that were an option. And in the rear: roll down windows, heat vent and sunshades.\n\n\nThe Carriage Room and Garage features vintage automobiles from the early 1900s as well as some old carriages.",
          "width": 4000,
          "height": 6000,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Dennis G. Jarvis",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DSC09026_-_1924_Dodge_Model_D2_Touring_Sedan_(36823715580).jpg",
